A vulnerability was fixed in DPDK.

Some downstream stakeholders were warned in advance in order to coordinate =
the
release of fixes and reduce the vulnerability window.

Problem:
A malicious container which has direct access to the vhost-user socket can =
keep
sending messages which may cause leaking resources until resulting a DOS.

All users of the vhost library are strongly encouraged to upgrade as soon as
possible.

CVE-2019-14818
Bugzilla: https://bugs.dpdk.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D363
Severity: Medium
CVSS scores: 6.8



